    "Black Market.Explanation": "Weapon variant chambered in both .300 Blackout and 5.56x45mm NATO rounds, featuring reduced recoil and improved ergonomics",
    "Black Market.ShortName": "B.Market",
    "Off-Meta.Name": "Off-Meta",
    "Off-Meta.Description": "A passionate modder's dream: made with care, time, and professional tools - on weapons long forgotten by the community",
    "Off-Meta.Explanation": "Weapon variant with reduced recoil and increased ergonomics. Some now support a wider variety of magazines, while others feature a no-bolt mode",
    "Off-Meta.ShortName": "Off-Meta",
    "Assault Rifle.Name": "Assault Rifle",
    "Assault Rifle.Description": "\"I want a refund! This weapon is way too big for me! B-but I like the caliber. Can you get me something smaller that can fit in my handbag?\"",
    "Assault Rifle.Explanation": "Pistol chambered in 5.56x45mm NATO, compatible with all M4A1 magazines",
    "Assault Rifle.ShortName": "AR",
    "Upgraded.Name": "Upgraded",
    "Upgraded.Description": "We took the original, cleaned it, tightened a few screws, and voilà - it's officially 'Upgraded' now!",
    "Upgraded.Explanation": "Weapon variant with improved recoil, accuracy, ergonomics, fire rate, and heat buildup",
    "Upgraded.ShortName": "Upgraded",
    "Light Machine Gun.Name": "Light Machine Gun",
    "Light Machine Gun.Description": "We're well aware that this magazine is either awkwardly floating beneath the weapon or somehow lodged inside it—but let's just call that a feature and move on",
    "Light Machine Gun.Explanation": "Weapon variant chambered in 7.62x54r ammunition, compatible only with a 100-round magazine. It features increased recoil, a lowered fire rate, and a full-auto fire mode exclusively",
    "Light Machine Gun.ShortName": "LMG",
    "Shotgun.Name": "Shotgun",
    "Shotgun.Description": "The perfect weapon to surprise your friends. They'll think you brought an assault rifle—until they see the magazine. That's when they know you're up to something sinister",
    "Shotgun.Explanation": "Weapon variant chambered in the 12/70 shotgun caliber, compatible with Saiga-12K magazines, but featuring increased recoil and a low fire rate",
    "Shotgun.ShortName": "Shotgun",
    "Unbreakable.Name": "Unbreakable",
    "Unbreakable.Description": "Some famous guy from television used his miracle product to make this gun unbreakable\nNow you can throw it into the sand without worrying about jams\n~It even works underwater!~\nJust... maybe don't cut it in half",
    "Unbreakable.Explanation": "Weapon variant immune to durability damage, overheating, and malfunctions",
    "Unbreakable.ShortName": "Unbreakable",
    "Hypersonic.Name": "Hypersonic",
    "Hypersonic.Description": "The technology used to modify this weapon shouldn't even work in theory. Decades of research have only managed to reduce the bullet's sensitivity to gravity and even that remains far from perfect",
    "Hypersonic.Explanation": "Weapon variant with exceptionally high muzzle velocity and very good accuracy",
    "Hypersonic.ShortName": "Hypersonic",
    "Sniper.Name": "Sniper",
    "Sniper.Description": "A weapon designed for hunters who occasionally mistake a human for a wild boar-from a comfortably safe distance",
    "Sniper.Explanation": "Shotgun weapon variant with increased velocity and accuracy",
    "Sniper.ShortName": "Sniper",
    "Speedy.Name": "Speedy",
    "Speedy.Description": "Gas gas gas! I'm gonna step on the gas Tonight I'll fly...",
    "Speedy.Explanation": "Weapon variant with an increased fire rate, but also higher recoil",
    "Speedy.ShortName": "Speedy",
    "No-Bolt.Name": "No-Bolt",
    "No-Bolt.Description": "Someone decided bolt-action rifles were too difficult to use, so they simply removed the bolt. Now it's no bolt, but plenty of action",
    "No-Bolt.Explanation": "Bolt action, but it is now DMR",
    "No-Bolt.ShortName": "No-Bolt",
    "FURY.Name": "FURY",
    "FURY.Description": "UNLEASH THE FURY OF TRASHY SMGs. THEY ARE NOW FURIOUS",
    "FURY.Explanation": "SMG variant chambered in .277 FURY (6.8x51mm), limited to a 2-shot burst fire mode",
    "FURY.ShortName": ".277",
    "Pocket-size.Name": "Pocket-size",
    "Pocket-size.Description": "Illegally small guns. Do not the gun",
    "Pocket-size.Explanation": "This weapon fits in one hand and can be equiped in holster slot. With a boost to ergonomics and almost weightless!",
    "Pocket-size.ShortName": "smol",
    "Rifle Grenade Launcher.Name": "Rifle Grenade Launcher",
    "Rifle Grenade Launcher.Description": "- It's like an underbarrel grenade launcher, but instead, it's an in-barrel grenade launcher!\n- You mean a rifle grenade…?\n- Exactly what I have in mind!",
    "Rifle Grenade Launcher.Explanation": "Weapon variant additionary chambered in 40mm grenades with slightly increased muzzle velocity. So, when you are out of ammo, just load grenade launcher rounds directly into the chamber!",
    "Rifle Grenade Launcher.ShortName": "R.Grenade",
    "Bombardier.Name": "Bombardier",
    "Bombardier.Description": "God has blessed this weapon with a very big... cylinder. And an absurd amount of firepower!",
    "Bombardier.Explanation": "A revolver that dreams of being a grenade launcher",
    "Bombardier.ShortName": "Bombardier",
    "Holster.Name": "Holster",
    "Holster.Description": "\"R&D inflated your pocket-dimension\" ~ADA",
    "Holster.Explanation": "SMG variant that trades its fire rate for more ergonomics and ability to be held in holster slot",
    "Holster.ShortName": "Holster",
    "Railgun.Name": "Railgun",
    "Railgun.Description": "Adding a secondary propellant charge to an already explosive grenade made it possible to reach nearly 450 m/s muzzle velocity from a weapon chambered in 40x46mm",
    "Railgun.Explanation": "Weapon variant chambered in 40x46mm grenades with unbelievable muzzle velocity, allowing grenades to be launched at nearly normal bullet speeds",
    "Railgun.ShortName": "Railgun",
    "Overclocked.Name": "Overclocked",
    "Overclocked.Description": "By harnessing water-cooling technology from high-performance PCs, this variant pushes your weapon to fire faster than ever before, delivering unmatched speed at the cost of increased complexity",
    "Overclocked.Explanation": "Weapon variant with an increased fire rate and enhanced cooling capabilities, but slightly reduced ergonomics",
    "Overclocked.ShortName": "OC",
    "Modified.Name": "Modified",
    "Modified.Description": "Upgraded to be a slightly better weapon, but its improved statistics come at the cost of sacrificing others",
    "Modified.Explanation": "Weapon variant in equilibrium with the universe, featuring adjustments to various aspects: reduced vertical recoil but increased horizontal recoil, improved ergonomics, lowered fire rate, increased heat buildup, and reduced weight",
    "Modified.ShortName": "Modified",
    "SMG.Name": "SMG",
    "SMG.Description": "A weapon for true gamblers—its fire rate depends entirely on how fast you can pull the trigger. Keep pulling, and eventually, you'll win",
    "SMG.Explanation": "Weapon variant chambered in 4.6x30mm HK caliber, featuring reduced recoil and an exceptionally high single-fire rate",
    "SMG.ShortName": "SMG",
    "Close Quarters.Name": "Close Quarters",
    "Close Quarters.Description": "PLACEHOLDER",
    "Close Quarters.Explanation": "Weapon variant chambered in 12.7x55mm caliber, featuring reduced recoil, fire rate and muzzle velocity",
    "Close Quarters.ShortName": "CQ",
    "20/70.Name": "20/70",
    "20/70.Description": "A typo in the weapon's description, left uncorrected out of sheer laziness. And now? Well, it's stuck like this-for better or for worse",
    "20/70.Explanation": "Shotgun variant chambered in 20ga shotgun cartridges",
    "20/70.ShortName": "20/70",
    "Shotgun-o-Revolver.Name": "Shotgun-o-Revolver",
    "Shotgun-o-Revolver.Description": "Somewhere, deep in the void of forbidden weapon concepts, someone asked: 'What if revolvers... but shotguns?",
    "Shotgun-o-Revolver.Explanation": "Revolver variant converted to fire shotgun shells. Because sometimes six big booms are better than six small ones",
    "Shotgun-o-Revolver.ShortName": "Shotgun-o",
    "World War II.Name": "World War II",
    "World War II.Description": "If your goal isn't to kill your enemies but to seriously injure them, this is the perfect weapon for you. Now with occasional WW2 flashbacks!",
    "World War II.Explanation": "Bootleg of the PPSh-41. It even has the same fire rate and immunity to malfunctions! On top of that, it boasts low recoil",
    "World War II.ShortName": "WW2",
    "Slav \"Thing\".Name": "Slav \"Thing\"",
    "Slav \"Thing\".Description": "If it works, don't question it. If it doesn't work, hit it with a wrench. Classic Slav engineering",
    "Slav \"Thing\".Explanation": "Weapon variant chambered in 7.62x39mm with increased stabilization point, increased recoil, dispersion and decreased ergonomics",
    "Slav \"Thing\".ShortName": "v2.0-Slav",
    "Freedom \"Thing\".Name": "Freedom \"Thing\"",
    "Freedom \"Thing\".Description": "If it works, don't question it. If it doesn't work, shoot it until it does. Classic American engineering",
    "Freedom \"Thing\".Explanation": "Weapon variant chambered in 5.56x45mm NATO with decreased recoil, increased ergonomics and fire rate but with increased stabilization point",
    "Freedom \"Thing\".ShortName": "v2.0-Freedom",
    "Smoothbore.Name": "Smoothbore",
    "Smoothbore.Description": "Technically not a rifle - at least according to someone’s paperwork. Modified to support civilian smoothbore cartridges while retaining most of the platform’s original handling. Whether that makes it legal, practical, or safe is another question entirely",
    "Smoothbore.Explanation": "Weapon variant capable of using both .366 TKM and 7.62x39mm ammunition",
    "Smoothbore.ShortName": "Smoothbore",
    "Panic.Name": "Panic",
    "Panic.Description": "Don't panic-it's just a cockroach... *bang* *bang* *bang*",
    "Panic.Explanation": "Shotguns limited to a MaxRounds Powermag 20-round magazine, featuring a full-auto fire mode, increased recoil, and a higher fire rate",
    "Panic.ShortName": "Panic",
    "Control-Fire.Name": "Control-Fire",
    "Control-Fire.Description": "A practice weapon for newly appointed PMCs eager to try legendary 'fullauto' fire mode. Unfortunately, they end up disappointed",
    "Control-Fire.Explanation": "Weapon variant with only a full-auto fire mode but offering better controllability due to a low fire rate and no recoil",
    "Control-Fire.ShortName": "Control",
    "Slowed.Name": "Slowed",
    "Slowed.Description": "A gun once tossed into a swamp... now fished out, but not without consequences. Its action speed has suffered a serious debuff",
    "Slowed.Explanation": "Weapon variant with extremely low ergonomics, fire rate, and velocity. Full-auto only, but with reduced recoil when sustained",
    "Slowed.ShortName": "Slowed",
    "Quick-scope.Name": "Quick-scope",
    "Quick-scope.Description": "Quick! Use this bolt-action as a close-quarters weapon, we don't have time!\nDon't ask any questions",
    "Quick-scope.Explanation": "Weapon variant with maximum ergonomics and extremely high velocity, restricted to one special reflex sight",
    "Quick-scope.ShortName": "Quick",
    "Converted.Name": "Converted",
    "Converted.Description": "We have successfully converted your weak-ass shotguns and pistols to the medium-ass assault rifles, or something, I don't care...",
    "Converted.Explanation": "Weapon variant chambered in 9x39mm caliber with increased durability burn",
    "Converted.ShortName": "Converted",
    "BFG-50.Name": "BFG-50",
    "BFG-50.Description": "\"The BFG-50 was Mark Serbu's first rifle design, coming into production in late 1999. It is on the civilian market for a price of $2,000-$3,000 USD, but is not intended to be used by any armed forces in the world\"\n~https://guns.fandom.com/wiki/Serbu_BFG-50",
    "BFG-50.Explanation": "Weapon variant chambered in .50 BMG with significantly increased recoil, slightly increased ergonomics and with only a 1-round magazine",
    "BFG-50.ShortName": "BFG-50",
    "No-Scope.Name": "No-Scope",
    "No-Scope.Description": "Do a 360 headshot with this!",
    "No-Scope.Explanation": "Weapon variant missing scope slot but with increased ergonomics and fire rate",
    "No-Scope.ShortName": "No-Scope",
    "Fullburst.Name": "Fullburst",
    "Fullburst.Description": "The trigger is broken and can get stuck, causing almost the entire magazine to unload with a single pull—or not, as it might jam in the meantime. Fullburst, but only sometimes",
    "Fullburst.Explanation": "Weapon variant with a 30-round burst fire mode only, featuring reduced fire rate and recoil, but with an increased chance of jamming due to higher heat buildup",
    "Fullburst.ShortName": "Fullburst",
    "Experimental.Name": "Experimental",
    "Experimental.Description": "They did everything to this weapon: touch it in forbidden places, pull the trigger with thumb, put vaseline in the barrel and paint it pink. Nightmare fuel!",
    "Experimental.Explanation": "Weapon variant with increased malfunction chanse but no misfire malfunction, increased durability burn, but with increased fire rate and no recoil. Features only full auto fire mode",
    "Experimental.ShortName": "Experimental",
    "Lawn Mower.Name": "Lawn Mower",
    "Lawn Mower.Description": "BRRRRRRRRRRRR - the grass is gone. The enemy is gone. Your hearing is gone",
    "Lawn Mower.Explanation": "A weapon variant with almost tripled fire rate, decreased recoil and no heat buildup, but with bad dispersion and bullet velocity",
    "Lawn Mower.ShortName": "BRRRR",
    "Pistol.Name": "Pistol",
    "Pistol.Description": "A weapon variant designed specifically for pistol quests, tailored for those who dislike using actual pistols",
    "Pistol.Explanation": "Bolt-action rifles with significantly improved accuracy and handling, but chambered in the 9x18mm pistol caliber",
    "Pistol.ShortName": "\"Pistol\"",
    "Desert.Name": "Desert",
    "Desert.Description": "A weapon variant designed specifically for pistol quests, tailored for those who dislike using actual pistols. Desert edition",
    "Desert.Explanation": "Bolt-action rifles with significantly improved accuracy and handling, but chambered in the 50AE pistol caliber",
    "Desert.ShortName": "\"Desert\"",
    "Laser Rifle.Name": "Laser Rifle",
    "Laser Rifle.Description": "\"That is the third time I am trying to make a Laser Rifle. Third time's a charm?\"\n*Clicking*\n\"It's not... oh, it was not on! Maybe now?\"\n*Small explosion*\n\"Oh, ffs!\"",
    "Laser Rifle.Explanation": "Weapon variant chambered in 9x21mm caliber ammo, shooting 3-bullet burst with incredible fire rate and increased muzzle velocity",
    "Laser Rifle.ShortName": "Laser",
    "Glass Cannon.Name": "Glass Cannon",
    "Glass Cannon.Description": "It's neither made of glass nor actually a cannon - but look at it. When you fire it, it's definitely a cannon, and when you check its durability, it's definitely glass",
    "Glass Cannon.Explanation": "Shotgun variant chambered in .50 BMG with a 1-round magazine. Features increased durability damage but can be held in the pistol slot",
    "Glass Cannon.ShortName": "Glass Cannon",
    "Early Prototype.Name": "Early Prototype",
    "Early Prototype.Description": "Developed as a proof-of-concept using the military-standard 7.62x54mmR cartridge. The abundance of compatible magazines made logistics simple during early trials",
    "Early Prototype.Explanation": "Weapon variant chambered in 7.62x54mmR that can use a larger variety of magazines",
    "Early Prototype.ShortName": "Prototype",

